// DISABLE_NATIVE: targetFamily=MINGW


// Leave-and-return staleness on the enum-ordinal axis (the open family pinned by the
// committed, still-failing corpus cases dependencies/dependentLibraryLeavesAndReturns,
// dependencies/propertyTypeChangedWhileDependentAbsent,
// dependencies/objcBoundClassMovedWhileDependentAbsent and
// dependencies/renamedFileWhileDependentOutOfLink):
//   step 0: lib1 declares enum class E { B, C }; lib2 lowers `when (e)` over it, baking
//           E's ordinals into its per-file cache (NativeEnumWhenLowering.mapConstEnumEntry
//           records a strong per-file dependency on the enum's file for exactly that reason
//           -- the KT-86110 fix, EnumClassLowering.kt:76). Everything is cached.
//   step 1: lib2 is OUT OF THE LINK while lib1 inserts NEW before B, shifting the ordinals
//           (B: 0 -> 1). lib1 is recompiled and re-cached, but CacheBuilder's change
//           detection walks only the libraries of the current link (CacheBuilder.kt:271),
//           so lib2's cache keeps its step-0 state.
//   step 2: lib2 returns with its byte-identical step-0 klib. No klib recompiles, so
//           changedFiles contains only main (its source was swapped back) and the dirty
//           dfs -- which starts only from changed/added/removed files (CacheBuilder.kt:344)
//           -- never walks lib2's recorded dependency edge lib2|w.kt -> lib1|e.kt. The
//           edge carries no version or hash of the dependency it was built against, and the
//           returning-library check staleCacheReason -> computeDependenciesFingerprint
//           (CacheBuilder.kt:145-170) deliberately excludes per-file cached dependencies
//           (CacheBuilder.kt:131-137: "changes in the per-file cached dependencies are
//           tracked by the dirty-file analysis" -- the very tracking that lost the step-1
//           change). IC therefore reuses lib2's stale when dispatch: E.B now has runtime
//           ordinal 1, which the old switch maps into the C branch, and the test fails
//           with Expected <b>, actual <c>. The clean link (fresh cache dir) rebuilds
//           lib2's w.kt against the new enum and passes, as does the non-IC link.
//
// A correct IC must re-walk a returning library's recorded per-file dependency edges
// against the dependencies' current cache state: `modified cache: w.kt` at step 2 is the
// fix. The sibling windows of the same root cause found by this campaign -- the itable
// (interface grows a default method) and the vtable (superclass grows a method) -- are
// kept as reduced scenarios under
// build/kn-ic-fuzz/c7-2026-11-08/r2t6-iface-growth-while-dependent-abs/reduce/manual and
// build/kn-ic-fuzz/c7-2026-11-08/r3t2-r3t2-vtable-slot-stale-when-subc/reduce/manual.

MODULES: lib1, lib2, main

STEP 0:
    libs: lib1, lib2, main

// lib2 is out of the link while its dependency lib1 changes.
STEP 1:
    libs: lib1, main

// lib2 returns; its klib and per-file cache are untouched.
STEP 2:
    libs: main
